## relwork searches.md: method, coverage, not searched (l.1-15, 61-92)
=== stability-relwork-2026-11-18/ledger/searches.md l.1-15 ===
1	# Searches: method, coverage, what was not searched, errata, and every query
2	
3	## Method
4	
5	- **Services.** All four need no account and allow automated queries.
6	  - INSPIRE (`inspirehep.net/api/literature`): title, fulltext and `refersto:recid:` citer queries, every page.
7	  - The arXiv API (`export.arxiv.org/api/query`): abstracts and titles, all categories, math included. 100 per page, at
8	    most three pages, 4 s between requests.
9	  - zbMATH Open (`api.zbmath.org`).
10	  - OpenAlex (`api.openalex.org`): seed works, citer sets, and relevance searches (top 200).
11	  - **Zenodo** (`zenodo.org/api/records`), the public record search.
12	    - Added in round 5, after OpenAlex's O05/O06 surfaced three Zenodo-only computer-assisted preprints that no other
13	      service had returned. 25 records per page is the anonymous limit.
14	    - Record metadata and file lists are saved as `cache/searches/zenodo_<id>.json`. PDFs were fetched from the record's
15	      file link (`tools/fetch_url.py`).
=== stability-relwork-2026-11-18/ledger/searches.md l.61-92 ===
61	## Positive controls
62	
63	Your S5, S6, S23, S28, S8, S14, S26, S9, S27 and S31 are seeds. Each also surfaced through queries other than its own
64	lookups and citer set (`screen/positive_controls.tsv`).
65	
66	## Coverage
67	
68	- **Citers beyond INSPIRE (message 14, Q1).** OpenAlex citer sets were taken in full for S5, S6, S23, S28, S8, S14, S26,
69	  S9, S27 and S31. The records found only through OpenAlex are counted in `screen/positive_controls.tsv`.
70	- **Weak spots.**
71	  - Title queries miss papers whose titles do not name the setting. The citer sets and fulltext queries are there to
72	    cover that.
73	  - INSPIRE's fulltext covers only INSPIRE-indexed papers, mostly hep, gr-qc and math-ph.
74	  - arXiv math full texts are not full-text searched by any service used. Abstracts were searched through the arXiv
75	    API, OpenAlex and zbMATH.
76	
77	## Not searched
78	
79	- **Google Scholar, ADS, MathSciNet.** They need an account or a subscription, or forbid automated access.
80	- **Semantic Scholar.** Not used. Message 14 asked for OpenAlex or Semantic Scholar, and the OpenAlex citer sets were
81	  complete.
82	- **OpenAlex deep paging with a key.**
83	  - Since 2026, OpenAlex refuses cursor paging past the first page without an API key (HTTP 401, OC01–OC03, page 2).
84	    An account was not created.
85	  - Basic paging (`page=2, 3`) needs no key, and all citer sets were then fetched in full (OC01b probe; OC01c, OC02b,
86	    OC03b).
87	- **Full texts of non-INSPIRE papers** beyond those fetched.
88	- **Other repositories.** Zenodo was searched only with N01b–N17. Other repositories that host unrefereed preprints
89	  (Research Square, Preprints.org, ESS Open Archive) were not searched directly. Some of their records came through
90	  OpenAlex and were screened by title.
91	- **Publisher-only sources.** None was needed. Dafermos's essay is open access at the publisher, and that copy was
92	  fetched.
