## zmode q1: closed forms at extremality found for other sectors (l.1-16, 39-47)
=== zmode-litcheck-2026-11-10/ledger/q1_static_solutions.md l.1-16 ===
1	# Q1: explicit static (ω = 0) solutions of the Kodama–Ishibashi master equations for charged, and extremal, higher-D black holes
2	
3	**Answer, relative to the sources below.** No closed-form static solution of the scalar-type master equations of a
4	charged black hole in D ≥ 5 was found, at extremality or at any other charge.
5	- **Found elsewhere in closed form:**
6	  - the tensor and vector types at extremality (Pereñiguez–Cardoso), and spin-0 test fields;
7	  - the neutral scalar type (Kodama 2004, Kol–Smolkin, Hui et al., the ladder papers);
8	  - in D = 4, RN at every charge (Rai–Santoni; two 2024–25 extremal papers).
9	- **Only numerically:** the charged scalar type in D ≥ 5. Xia–Ma–Pang (2025) solve the static scalar-type equations of
10	  D-dimensional RN at q/µ = 0.1, and they write that these Love numbers "have not been studied" before.
11	- **Only near the horizon, as scaling exponents:** static deformations of extremal RN in D dimensions (Horowitz et al.;
12	  Chen–de Rham–Tolley; Chen–Kovács).
13	- **Confidence:** medium-high for D ≥ 5. The negative rests on 93 generic queries (`searches.md`) and on reading the
14	  papers below. It is not a proof of absence.
15	
16	**D = 4.** Z covers D ≥ 4, and the 4D literature has general analytic static solutions for RN at every charge. I did not
